# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 7 (stage A, 2026-10-18). Played lives only.
# Moments: losing your job, the cyclist at dusk, a holiday romance, the farewell at the barracks fence, a close friend
# moves away, the street starts its own watch, the last week of the painkillers, the congregation splits in two, moving
# to a smaller home or into care, facing the end, a wedding without the old rite, a frightening diagnosis.
# Each first bold way has its links (well and badly), each with its own
# bold way. Colours: W 8, U 8, B 8, R 9, G 8; chances 30, 35, 40 and 45 about twice in each colour.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- losing your job

== bold: losing your job / U
base: take stock of your skills and retrain for a field that is growing
likelier_if: has [school-leaving certificate] +5; has [working with data] +10; mark 'learned a skill' +5
- U | spend the whole payout on a hard coding course, and bet the year on it | v: self-direction, achievement | act: spend the whole payout on a hard coding course and bet the year on it | chance: 35 | grants: writing code | title_if_fails: out of work
works: {N} works through the course at the kitchen table every night, and by spring writes code that runs.
works: The course is brutal, but {N} comes out the other side able to write code, and it shows in every test.
fails: The course goes over {Ns} head by the second month, the payout is gone, and {N} is still out of work.
fails: {N} drops out halfway with the money spent and no work in sight, and the months out of work stretch on.

== bold: losing your job / G
base: move in with family, and work cash in hand for people you know
likelier_if: years [family business] 5 +10; has [old family name] +5
- G | take over the family's old shop, and keep the family name over the door | v: tradition, security | act: take over the family's old shop and keep the family name over the door | chance: 30 | requires: family business | title: shop owner | takes_if_fails: family business
works: {N} takes the keys from {parent}, and the shop opens on Monday with {N} behind the counter as its owner.
works: The old customers come back one by one, and the shop is {Ns} now, name over the door and all.
fails: The shop loses money every month, and by winter the family sells it to strangers.
fails: {N} cannot make the old shop pay, and the family business that fed three generations closes for good.

