earth: the firm that let you go has a system nobody can fix, and your old boss asks you to come back and fix it
scene: The firm that let {N} go is in trouble: its booking system has broken, and nobody left can fix it. {boss} rings to ask if {N} would come in for a few weeks.
scene gone: {boss} has left the firm, but {colleague} rings instead: the system is broken, and {N} is the only one who knows both the work and the code.
- W | agree a fair fee in writing, and fix exactly what they ask | v: conformity, security | act: agree a fair fee in writing and fix exactly what the firm asks | chance: 78
- U | find out why it broke before touching a line of it | v: self-direction | chance: 75
- B | charge them twice the going rate, and make them wait a week | v: power, achievement | act: charge the firm twice the going rate and make it wait a week | chance: 70
- R | tell your old boss what being let go felt like, then say no | v: self-direction | act: tell the old boss what being let go felt like, then say no | chance: 80
- G | do it for the sake of the old team who are still there | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 76
works: The system runs again, and {N} walks out of the old building with a fair cheque and a straight back.
works: Old colleagues buy {N} a drink, and the bad feeling from the layoff finally lifts.
fails: The fix takes far longer than promised, and {boss} starts to sound like a boss again.
fails: {N} spends the weeks in the old building feeling like the one who was let go.
works gone: The system runs again, and {N} walks out of the old building with a fair cheque and a straight back.
works gone: The old team buys {N} a drink, and the bad feeling from the layoff finally lifts.
fails gone: The fix takes far longer than promised, and the firm starts to treat {N} like staff again.
fails gone: {N} spends the weeks in the old building feeling like the one who was let go.

